         "title": "Anthony Gonçalves: “Worst thing you could do to a Portuguese person, is tell them they can't do something”",
         "description": "<p><span>From nightclub promoter to chef-patron, Anthony Gonçalves has spent a lifetime reinventing himself, and today he serves as living proof that Portuguese cuisine belongs on the world's fine dining stage. In a conversation recorded at his Westchester restaurant Canopy, the self-taught chef sat down with Heart & Hustle host Anthony Gonçalves, his namesake, with whom he has been confused for 25 years, to trace a path from the streets of Yonkers to a family kitchen that spans three generations</span></p>",
